    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63-a1">

                <pb facs="0209" n="85" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg85"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    60.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Prado to Mr.
                            Adams</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Relations of Bolivia</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1881-02-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 1, 1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to your
                    excellency the original and a legalized copy of a diplomatic circular<anchor
                        n="*" xml:id="d63-f1"/> which this office directs to that of the United
                    States, and in which, by occasion of the new defeat which the allied armies have
                    suffered, it again expresses the unalterable intention of Bolivia to defend its
                    rights and repel the ideas of conquest entertained by Chili.</p>
                <p>Meanwhile I beg of your excellency to please have it reach its high destination,
                    and accept the sentiments of my most perfect consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>DANIEL N. DEL PRADO.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
